-- title:
--   Bezoutian determinant multiplies to the Jacobian determinant
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $m$ a natural number, and $f \colon \mathrm{Fin}\ m \to R[x_0,\dots,x_{m-1}]$ a family of $m$ polynomials in $m$ variables. Let $a$ be an $m \times m$ matrix of elements $a_{ij}$ of $R[x] \otimes_R R[x]$ satisfying, for every $i$, the Bezoutian identity $f_i \otimes 1 - 1 \otimes f_i = \sum_j a_{ij}\,(X_j \otimes 1 - 1 \otimes X_j)$ in $R[x] \otimes_R R[x]$. Write $I = (\,\mathrm{span}\ \mathrm{range}\ f\,)$ for the ideal generated by the $f_i$ and $\pi \colon R[x] \to R[x]/I$ for the quotient map. Then the image of $\det(a_{ij})$ under the algebra map $\pi \otimes \pi \colon R[x] \otimes_R R[x] \to (R[x]/I) \otimes_R (R[x]/I)$, followed by the multiplication algebra map $\mathrm{Algebra.TensorProduct.lmul'}$ of $R[x]/I$ onto itself, equals $\pi\bigl(\det(\partial f_i/\partial x_j)\bigr)$, the class modulo $I$ of the Jacobian determinant of $f$.
--
--   This is the Scheja–Storch identity comparing the Bezoutian of a square presentation with its Jacobian determinant: the multiplication map carries the diagonal class $\bar\Delta$ to the Jacobian class $\bar J$ in $A = R[x]/(f)$. It is used in the construction of the Scheja–Storch trace form, namely in [`Algebra.exists_dual_bijective_mul_and_trace_eq_jacobianDet_mul_of_square_presentation`](thm.html#Algebra.exists_dual_bijective_mul_and_trace_eq_jacobianDet_mul_of_square_presentation).
